 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "How can anyone trust seventeen million lines that no human has read in full?",
   "start": 0.725,
   "end": 5.312
  },
  {
   "text": "In Lean, every step must follow from earlier ones by fixed rules,",
   "start": 5.312,
   "end": 9.625
  },
  {
   "text": "and a small program, the kernel, checks them all.",
   "start": 9.625,
   "end": 13.012
  },
  {
   "text": "Kevin Buzzard lists four questions to ask of AI-written Lean.",
   "start": 13.012,
   "end": 16.825
  },
  {
   "text": "Is the statement right?",
   "start": 17.725,
   "end": 19.038
  },
  {
   "text": "Here it's the definition in Mathlib, Lean's shared library,",
   "start": 19.038,
   "end": 22.2
  },
  {
   "text": "written by people and vetted by experts.",
   "start": 22.2,
   "end": 24.725
  },
  {
   "text": "Does it compile?",
   "start": 24.725,
   "end": 25.812
  },
  {
   "text": "Dozens of people have rebuilt it.",
   "start": 25.812,
   "end": 27.65
  },
  {
   "text": "Does it prove exactly that statement, using only the standard axioms?",
   "start": 27.65,
   "end": 31.562
  },
  {
   "text": "Two independent tools say yes.",
   "start": 31.562,
   "end": 33.725
  },
  {
   "text": "Could it exploit a bug in Lean itself?",
   "start": 33.725,
   "end": 36.088
  },
  {
   "text": "Several independent checkers accepted it, two of them with a formal proof,",
   "start": 36.088,
   "end": 39.987
  },
  {
   "text": "relative to set theory, that they can't accept a false one.",
   "start": 39.987,
   "end": 43.475
  },
  {
   "text": "That is the basis of the November twenty-first statement of full confidence.",
   "start": 44.4,
   "end": 49.05
  }
 ],
 "cues": {
